From 18bb85cb5abb9c1540f656bcce474d7108f72acd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:09:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the resynchronization of the FEL layer after a
 drain says why

In the hardware test of 1.0 RC4, after a seek over a slow network, the log
said "DV FEL: resynchronizing the enhancement layer (unknown)", and 19
pictures went out without the FEL residual until the next random-access
point common to both layers. dvbridge_fel_submit() refuses a base packet
while the layer is drained (the video thread squeezes the pictures out of
the decoders when the stream runs dry), and gave no reason, so the decoder's
resynchronization said "unknown". It says now that a base packet came while
the layer was drained. Nothing else changes: whether the layer can go on at
such a packet without waiting for the next random-access point is a separate
question (read, not changed here).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
index c866ac6..cf52e5e 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
@@ -1356,6 +1356,11 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
     f->recent[f->submitted % BASE_TIMES_MAX].pts = packet->pts;
     f->recent[f->submitted % BASE_TIMES_MAX].seq = f->submitted;
     f->recent[f->submitted % BASE_TIMES_MAX].rpu = rpu == DVBRIDGE_RPU_NO_RESIDUAL || rpu == DVBRIDGE_RPU_RESIDUAL;
+    /* Hades: a base packet that comes while the layer is drained (the video thread squeezes the
+     * pictures out of the decoders when the stream runs dry) ends the drain by starting the layer
+     * again: said so, where the log said "unknown" */
+    if (f->draining && !f->failed && !f->reason)
+        f->reason = "a base packet came while the layer was drained (the stream had run dry)";
     if (f->failed || f->draining)
         return false;
     /* By picture order every base packet needs its time, which an enhancement picture takes.
